    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what I fixed:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Problem:** The `frai gate init --ci` command was not creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` workflow file, even though `frai-gate init --ci` (run directly) worked correctly.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `--ci` flag was defined on the parent `frai` program, not on the `gate` subcommand. When the user ran `frai gate init --ci`, Commander parsed the flag at the parent level and never passed it to the `gate` subcommand's action handler.\n\n**Solution:** Modified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Store a reference to the program instance in a module-level variable\n2. Access the parent program's options in the `gate` command action using `programInstance.opts()`\n3. Forward the `--ci` flag to the frai-gate CLI if it's present\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- Added `let programInstance: Command;` before `main()`\n- Stored the program instance: `programInstance = program;`\n- Modified the gate action to check for and forward the `--ci` flag to spawnSync\n\n**Verification:** Tested with `node packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci` and confirmed:\n- \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` is created\n- \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` is now created\n- \u2705 No errors occur\n\nThe package has been rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build` and is ready for use.",
